1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:05,409
In Department Settings, find Address and
Default Map Center GPS Coordinates.

2
00:00:05,789 --> 00:00:09,789
Our fictional training department has a
complete latitude and longitude pair.

3
00:00:10,149 --> 00:00:14,810
The page explains that an explicit center
takes precedence over address geocoding.

4
00:00:15,310 --> 00:00:17,670
Read the saved values before changing
them.

5
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:21,459
A department map center is a viewing
reference; it does not

6
00:00:21,459 --> 00:00:23,489
establish a unit's current position.

7
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:27,829
This recording reviews the existing center
without changing or saving it.

8
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:31,879
Open Mapping and enter Engine in Filter
marker text.

9
00:00:32,279 --> 00:00:34,110
Two named engine markers remain.

10
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:38,510
The training fixture includes positions in
different states, so this is a

11
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:42,109
filter demonstration rather than a local
response recommendation.

12
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:44,340
Filtering changes this map view.

13
00:00:44,709 --> 00:00:48,739
It does not rename resources, remove
calls, or establish that a

14
00:00:48,739 --> 00:00:50,799
displayed unit is ready to respond.

15
00:00:50,959 --> 00:00:53,870
Clear the text filter and check Hide
labels.

16
00:00:54,239 --> 00:00:57,369
The marker symbols remain while their name
labels disappear.

17
00:00:57,760 --> 00:01:00,619
This can reduce clutter when several
objects overlap.

18
00:01:01,119 --> 00:01:04,529
Restore the labels while learning
unfamiliar symbols, and use the

19
00:01:04,529 --> 00:01:08,400
category controls to decide which kinds of
objects you want to inspect.

20
00:01:08,589 --> 00:01:12,769
Uncheck Show units and adjust the zoom to
see the three training calls.

21
00:01:13,110 --> 00:01:16,420
The unit markers disappear from this view
while the calls remain.

22
00:01:16,950 --> 00:01:20,589
When a resource seems missing, check the
text filter and category

23
00:01:20,589 --> 00:01:22,790
visibility before changing its record.

24
00:01:23,169 --> 00:01:25,070
Restore Show units afterward.

25
00:01:25,549 --> 00:01:29,180
Visibility in a map is separate from an
object's saved location

26
00:01:29,209 --> 00:01:30,670
and operational status.

27
00:01:30,870 --> 00:01:34,530
Return to the map controls and open Manage
POIs.

28
00:01:35,019 --> 00:01:37,660
This department initially has no point
types.

29
00:01:38,089 --> 00:01:41,810
Add POI Type creates a category for
related points.

30
00:01:42,190 --> 00:01:45,520
A department might organize staging
locations, search assembly

31
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:49,549
points, security rally points, contractor
access points, or

32
00:01:49,549 --> 00:01:51,449
industrial response destinations.

33
00:01:51,910 --> 00:01:54,720
Choose a category name that its users will
recognize.

34
00:01:54,919 --> 00:01:56,999
Name the type Academy Staging.

35
00:01:57,520 --> 00:02:01,289
Check Is Destination to identify this
category as potential

36
00:02:01,289 --> 00:02:03,550
destinations for a person or unit.

37
00:02:03,989 --> 00:02:06,340
Review Color, Marker and Icon.

38
00:02:06,709 --> 00:02:09,940
We retain the blue default color and
standard pin, with

39
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:11,869
no symbol selected under Icon.

40
00:02:12,330 --> 00:02:16,640
A destination category describes a point's
intended use; it does not

41
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:20,750
verify that a location is accessible or
suitable for a real deployment.

42
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:23,060
Scroll to the preview and save control.

43
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:28,369
This example has no custom image, and the
form says the default marker is used.

44
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:32,199
The preview helps review appearance, but
it is still a form.

45
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:37,699
Choose Add POI Type to save the category,
then read the result in the list.

46
00:02:37,899 --> 00:02:42,760
The list now contains Academy Staging, the
saved blue color, Destination

47
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:44,820
Yes, and a point count of zero.

48
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:47,850
View opens the category's information and
map.

49
00:02:48,239 --> 00:02:50,329
Add creates an individual point in it.

50
00:02:50,810 --> 00:02:52,369
Choose Add for this example.

51
00:02:52,779 --> 00:02:55,870
The separate Import control is visible,
but this walkthrough

52
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:57,329
creates the point manually.

53
00:02:57,570 --> 00:03:02,059
Enter the latitude and longitude in their
separate fields, using decimal notation.

54
00:03:02,570 --> 00:03:06,589
Name this record Academy Staging Point,
enter a clearly fictional

55
00:03:06,589 --> 00:03:10,499
address, and add a note identifying it as
an exercise location.

56
00:03:10,969 --> 00:03:15,310
Review the coordinate signs and the
point's purpose, then choose Add POI.

57
00:03:16,089 --> 00:03:20,380
For community paramedicine and mental
health teams, use permitted operational

58
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:24,720
destinations and keep sensitive visit
details out of general map notes.

59
00:03:24,909 --> 00:03:28,899
In the category's List tab, check the
saved name, address,

60
00:03:29,090 --> 00:03:31,269
note, latitude and longitude.

61
00:03:31,729 --> 00:03:33,770
The list now contains one entry.

62
00:03:34,140 --> 00:03:36,329
Compare the coordinate pair with what you
entered.

63
00:03:36,650 --> 00:03:40,810
A successful navigation alone is not
enough; this stored row gives

64
00:03:40,810 --> 00:03:42,720
you the actual values to verify.

65
00:03:43,130 --> 00:03:45,269
Select Edit to reopen the record.

66
00:03:45,510 --> 00:03:49,039
The Edit POI form reopens with the saved
values.

67
00:03:49,519 --> 00:03:52,220
Check the record identity and both
coordinates before

68
00:03:52,220 --> 00:03:53,820
making any future change.

69
00:03:54,169 --> 00:03:56,210
This recording only reads them back.

70
00:03:56,700 --> 00:04:00,690
Save POI is available for a deliberate
edit, but we return to

71
00:04:00,690 --> 00:04:02,489
Mapping without changing the point.

72
00:04:02,669 --> 00:04:09,009
On the operating map, filter for Academy
Staging Point and keep Show POIs checked.

73
00:04:09,429 --> 00:04:13,039
The actual saved marker and its name are
now visible on the map.

74
00:04:13,450 --> 00:04:16,190
Compare its position with recognizable
surroundings.

75
00:04:16,570 --> 00:04:20,049
A saved coordinate can be plotted
accurately and still describe the

76
00:04:20,049 --> 00:04:24,709
wrong intended location, so review the
placement before operational use.

77
00:04:24,950 --> 00:04:27,070
Open the marker to inspect its popup.

78
00:04:27,530 --> 00:04:30,530
Check the point name and its Academy
Staging category.

79
00:04:30,930 --> 00:04:34,069
Use the saved List or Edit view when you
need to review the

80
00:04:34,069 --> 00:04:36,289
complete note or exact coordinates.

81
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:40,800
This connection between a named record and
its actual map position is useful

82
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:45,310
for search teams, security departments,
wildland contractors and industrial

83
00:04:45,310 --> 00:04:47,740
teams as well as fire and EMS.

84
00:04:47,910 --> 00:04:52,550
Uncheck Show POIs while retaining the
point's name in the text filter.

85
00:04:52,959 --> 00:04:54,149
The marker disappears.

86
00:04:54,539 --> 00:04:56,600
This does not delete the saved point.

87
00:04:57,020 --> 00:05:01,079
If a dispatcher cannot find a known
location, this is one concrete

88
00:05:01,079 --> 00:05:04,350
visibility setting to check before
creating a duplicate record.

89
00:05:04,559 --> 00:05:06,260
Check Show POIs again.

90
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:10,679
The same saved marker returns without
recreating or editing it.

91
00:05:11,049 --> 00:05:14,429
Clear the text filter when you want the
broader operating picture.

92
00:05:14,809 --> 00:05:19,410
Keep a responsible owner for reviewing
destination names, notes and coordinates

93
00:05:19,450 --> 00:05:21,369
as department operations change.

94
00:05:21,559 --> 00:05:26,409
Open Map Icon Legend and find Stations,
hydrants and points of interest.

95
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:29,300
Academy Staging now appears in that group.

96
00:05:29,830 --> 00:05:34,290
The legend explicitly states that these
icons do not change with status.

97
00:05:34,690 --> 00:05:38,780
Keep this distinction clear: a staging
point is a place, while

98
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:42,419
a responding unit or member has a separate
operational status.

99
00:05:42,829 --> 00:05:46,800
A location marker alone does not tell you
who is available to use it.

